<title>UK: European VGO steady, arb to U.S workable.</title>
<headline>European VGO steady, arb to U.S workable.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>bid/ask	prev bid/ask</p>
<p> Low sulphur cargoes fob NWE	  137/139	  137/140</p>
<p> High sulphur cargoes fob NWE	 127/129	  126/128</p>
<p> High sulphur barges fob ARA	  130/132	  130/132</p>
<p> Formula quotation fob Med	     20/25	    20/25</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Vacuum gas oil was broadly steady in Europe on Friday. A deal was heard concluded at $138 fob NWE for a 50,000 tonne cargo of low sulphur material which traders expected to head transatlantic.</p>
<p>&quot;There had been rather optimisic talk of $142, but I think this trade puts that to bed,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>There was some market talk that $136 fob NWE had been done on Thursday, but news of the $138 deal led many in the market to question the earlier level.</p>
<p>High sulphur vgo was quieter than low sulphur with Russian material building up in NWE.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
</text>
